# local-llm-chat project rule

This repository configures **local Ollama coding models** and integrations (VS Code Local AI: Continue + Cline, Cursor, Codegraph, Headroom) on Windows without admin when possible.

## Required reading for setup tasks

- `AGENTS.md`
- `FEATURES.md`
- `docs/agent-setup-playbook.md`

## Machine setup

When asked to set up local models or this repo on a machine, run or guide:

```powershell
.\scripts\Setup-Machine.ps1 -Tier Auto
```

Use `-Tier 8GB`, `16GB`, or `32GB` from the user's RAM. Prefer scripts in `scripts/` over ad-hoc commands. After setup, run `.\scripts\Test-LocalSetup.ps1` and `.\scripts\Show-SetupStatus.ps1` if needed. First-time flows are documented as Cases A–O in `README.md`.

`Setup-Machine.ps1` also wires editors when possible:

- Cursor install + Models → Ollama (`Install-Cursor.ps1` / `Install-CursorConfig.ps1`)
- VS Code Local AI → Ollama (`Install-VSCodeLocalAI.ps1` / alias `Install-VSCodeConfig.ps1` — Continue chat + Cline agent)

Notable helpers:

- `Install-Cursor.ps1` — check / per-user install (unless `-SkipCursor`)
- `Install-CursorConfig.ps1` — find Cursor + write Models → Ollama into `state.vscdb`, disable cloud/catalog models (**quit Cursor first**; `-KeepRemoteModels` to keep remotes; unless `-SkipCursorConfig`)
- `Install-VSCode.ps1` — check / per-user install VS Code
- `Install-VSCodeLocalAI.ps1` — Continue (ChatGPT-like) + Cline (Cursor-like agent) + `Test-VSCodeSetup.ps1`
- `Test-VSCodeSetup.ps1` — full Case H check (extensions, Continue, Cline, MCP, local-only); alias `Test-VSCodeOllama.ps1`
- `Disable-RemoteAIProviders.ps1` — block OpenAI/Cursor/Grok/Copilot/etc. for Cursor + VS Code (+ Ollama cloud)
- `Install-ContinueConfig.ps1` / `Install-ClineConfig.ps1` — pieces of Case H
- `Install-Codegraph.ps1` — **fnm preferred** → npm Codegraph → agent install → **Cursor + VS Code mcp.json** → `codegraph init`; system npm only if fnm fails (`-RequireFnm` / `-SkipFnm` / `-WriteWorkspaceMcp`)
- `Install-GpuDrivers.ps1` / `Test-GpuSupport.ps1` — GPU + VM guidance
- Pull/download scripts skip models already on disk unless `-Force` (or `Update-CodingModels.ps1`)

## Constraints

- Do not commit `.gguf`, `models/**` blobs, or API/HF tokens.
- Only download models from sources in `docs/trusted-sources.md`.
- Ollama is the primary runtime; do not switch the stack to LM Studio unless asked.
- After setup, verify `ollama list` and `http://localhost:11434/api/tags`. Confirm editor rows in `Show-SetupStatus.ps1` (H/H-cfg/H-agent, I/I-cfg, L-vscode). Run `Test-VSCodeSetup.ps1` / `Test-CursorOllama.ps1`. Re-run `Install-VSCodeLocalAI.ps1` or `Install-CursorConfig.ps1` if needed (see `docs/integrations.md`).
